.TH XYNOOSD 1 "November 2026" "Xynoos HyperCore" "System Daemon"
.SH NAME
xynoosd \- XYNOOS HyperCore continuous self-tuning daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xynoosd
.RI "[options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
xynoosd is the dedicated autonomous continuous daemon for XYNOOS HyperCore.
It provides real-time multi-resource monitoring, non-invasive workload classification,
and adaptive policy coordination with strict starvation protection and oscillation prevention.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode observe-only|advisory|transactional
Operating mode for the daemon. Defaults to observe-only.
.TP
.B \-\-interval-ms N
Base polling interval in milliseconds.
.TP
.B \-\-max-cycles N
Terminate after N cycles (used for bounded testing and diagnostics).
.TP
.B \-\-pid-file PATH
Path to PID file.
.TP
.B \-\-no-pid-file
Do not write a PID file.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Query status of active daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-human
Output diagnostics in human-readable format instead of JSON.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xynoos (1)
